@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/streams/
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceStreamController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Background performers\nexact scope leases + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/streams/
alt It 's a normal flow . (without direct_user_uuid)
    API -> DB: STREAM + TOPIC By default + owner's binding
else Direct flow (Other user)
    API -> DB: Forced private=true\nDetermined pair + two unique user bindings
else flow with itself. (direct_user_uuid == owner)
    API -> DB: Forced private=true\nOnly one owner binding to the stream/topic
end
API -> DB: Add a record to the transactional outbox
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: the event that was recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: immutable topic_membership_policy_rebuild /\nfolder_projection / read_counters\n- I 'm not sure . outbox event -> One . task
Worker -> Worker: claim exact scope; For the topic work\nMESSAGE.created_at DESC
Worker -> Projection: linking the user to the stream/topic/folder
Worker -> Events: stream.created + folder.updated\natomically in one. DB transaction with a projection
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
@enduml
